      "worked_solution": "Since $B$ is the midpoint of $\\overset{―}{AD}$, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =\\frac{1}{2}AD \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 29 \\\\  & =14.5\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by the segment addition postulate, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =BC+CD \\\\ 14.5 & =BC+6.5 \\\\ 14.5-6.5 & =BC \\\\ BC & =8\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
